From: Yaw diagnostic field session (issue #13)
Subject: [Fix 2] actuator_node — loosen /wheel_odom vyaw covariance 0.0001 -> 0.01

Effect: lowers the EKF's trust in wheel-derived yaw rate, so IMU vyaw
wins the velocity-level fusion. EKF integrated yaw then tracks IMU
absolute yaw measurements instead of wheel-integrated yaw.

Apply with:    git apply docs/yaw_diag_patches/fix2_wheel_odom_vyaw_cov.patch
Revert with:   git apply -R docs/yaw_diag_patches/fix2_wheel_odom_vyaw_cov.patch

After applying, rebuild on the Jetson:
    cd ~/IGVC && colcon build --symlink-install --packages-select avros_control
    source install/setup.bash

Apply order: try Fix 1 alone first (config-only, no rebuild). If Test A
still shows EKF ≈ wheel, then add Fix 2 (this patch).

---
diff --git a/src/avros_control/avros_control/actuator_node.py b/src/avros_control/avros_control/actuator_node.py
--- a/src/avros_control/avros_control/actuator_node.py
+++ b/src/avros_control/avros_control/actuator_node.py
@@ -300,7 +300,7 @@ class ActuatorNode(Node):
         self._twist_cov[14] = 1e6     # vz
         self._twist_cov[21] = 1e6     # vroll
         self._twist_cov[28] = 1e6     # vpitch
-        self._twist_cov[35] = 0.0001  # vyaw
+        self._twist_cov[35] = 0.01    # vyaw (loosened for issue #13 — see docs/yaw_diag_patches/)

         # ---- threads / timers ----
         self._running = True
